1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
In a quiet forest, an oak tree stood tall and proud.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,000
It looked down on the small bamboo shoots growing nearby and said,

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,000
look how strong I am. No storm can break me.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
You, on the other hand, are weak and fragile.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,000
The bamboo simply replied, we'll see when the storm comes.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Seasons passed. One day, a fierce storm rolled through the forest.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The wind howled and the sky turned dark.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The mighty oak resisted, standing firm, but the stronger the wind blew,

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
the harder it fought. Eventually, with a great crack,

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:39,000
the oak broke and fell to the ground. The bamboo, however, bent with the wind.

11
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,000
It swayed and danced, bending so low it almost touched the ground.

12
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
But it never snapped. When the storm passed, the bamboo stood tall again.

13
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Strength isn't just about standing tall, it's about knowing when to bend,

14
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,000
when to be flexible and when to adapt. Life will bring storms,

15
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,000
but if you stay grounded and learn to bend instead of break,

16
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,000
you'll survive and thrive.

